and well, this opportunity

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:14.060
that's why I'm here, because of my passion for software development that brought me here

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.880
 

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:19.380
 

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:23.060
well, english I have learned it since I was a kid

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.560
 

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.720
when I was a kid, my parents made it possible for me to have a private teacher

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.740
for english classes

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:32.380
I remember I was about 9 years old

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.400
and also since that age

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.700
approximately 9 or 10 years

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.840
I was attending what we call a "bilingual" school

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.120
basically in latin-american countries

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.720
you will find schools

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.520
that will teach english

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.600
there you can find teachers that

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.040
have a high proficiency on English

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.180
and even teachers that are native English speakers

00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:00.700
and topics or courses

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:01.195
 

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.660
will be taught in english

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:08.940
so at that young age we are strongly exposed exposed to english to learn it

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:10.360
and that's how I learned

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:16.760
later, when I was studying at the university, we didn't have many courses in english

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:17.260
 

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:22.020
however I already had that knowledge from when I was a kid and teenager

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:23.120
 

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.280
so the things currently do for it

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:30.600
is just like watching TV and movies

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.095
 

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.940
without subtitles and in english

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.740
and that helps me to keep my english fresh

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.820
although right know I have the opportunity to speak it all the time because I'm living in Seattle

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:46.720
but anyways, is just a bit of advice of something I do to keep my english tuned

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:51.040
especially when I lived in Mexico where I wasn't exposed to english on a daily basis

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.040
 

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.200
 

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:01.120
the adaptation phase is something that has always been hard

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:01.680
 

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.680
the first thing that has been hard for me to adapt, and that I keep working on it

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:09.860
is naturally the language and communication

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.680
to put this in perspective

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.720
if I was at Mexico

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.480
I was living in a city called Guadalajara

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.580
and also lived in Mexico city

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:25.280
and, there are many particular ways to express yourself and communicate even in spanish

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.360
 

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:29.440
like those "slangs" how people call them

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.180
those "expressions"

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:33.660
and basically

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.380
when you go from one place to another

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.480
were costumes change a bit, even if its the same language

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.500
if I had moved to a different city

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.480
I would probably had to go through an adaptation fase

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:49.480
because even words start to change

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:52.640
maybe "A" doesn't mean "A" anymore, but it means "B"

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:55.660
and I know this because when I lived in Colombia

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.660
and I moved to Mexico

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:02.240
I had to go adapt, because a lot of times, even with the same language

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.060
 

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.760
I couldn't understand other people

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:09.160
I also experienced this for 6 months studying in Spain

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:14.700
also I didn't understood some people, even when it was the same language, Spanish

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:15.200
 

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:18.960
because it was spoken differently, different words were used

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:22.820
Now imagine this with english in the US

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:23.360
 

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.400
we have the factor of costumes

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.200
but also language

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:31.920
plus being talking in a different language all the time

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:35.700
I was exhausted because I wasn't used to do it all day long

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:40.880
and that obviously started to affect they way I communicated with my colleagues

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:44.000
I had to put a lot of attention of what was being said

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:48.500
Had to review anything discussed in meetings

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.160
 

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.020
asking multiple times to a colleague what was said

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.520
just to make sure that I could understand things at 100%

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:58.220
so that was the first thing I started

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:01.820
to struggle a bit in this adaptation process

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.740
the second thing, was mostly in the technical aspect

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:09.880
obviously for me, starting at Amazon was a leap in technical skills

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.940
required to be able to do my work, and

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.120
 

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:20.980
what can I tell you, I have to learn something everyday which is very exciting

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.520
but when I see the level of skill that people have

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.640
I have had to put more effort than usual

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:30.020
more than I considered "normal" effort

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.940
so that I can get to the same level as my peers

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:36.580
it started being a daily struggle, but little by little, moving forward

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.220
is like

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.440
is very reassuring when you start feeling that

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.800
you are now able to do things that have value for the team

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.800
However getting there has been difficult for me, even now

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.920
 

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:53.920
and I think it's part of the adaptation because doing this, is also

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.780
linked with communication

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.700
it's not the same thing adapting and ramp up

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.000
uhm, in your native language

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.040
than doing it in a different language, so everything is connected

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:09.260
 

00:15:09.525 --> 00:15:12.645
 

00:15:12.645 --> 00:15:14.880
 

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.080
well the visa thing in detail is super complicated

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:20.420
but basically what they are

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.660
it's a piece of paper, a document

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:26.620
is some kind of permit that a country provides you in order to

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:29.320
be able to visit that country, this if you are not originally from that country

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.300
the United states is a country for which

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.460
some other countries require a visa

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.200
permission so that you can access

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.120
or visit it legally

00:15:40.125 --> 00:15:43.200
and there are visas of many types, there are tourist visas..

00:15:43.205 --> 00:15:46.265
..visas for students

00:15:46.265 --> 00:15:49.540
there are also work visas, among other kinds of visas

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:52.580
so for a person like myself

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.715
 

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.840
holding both Mexican and Colombian citizenships

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:59.180
I had different options.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:02.020
Mexicans and Canadias for isntance, can apply to a special visa

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.160
named TN visa

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.720
that belongs to the NAFTA agreement between these 3 countries

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.500
you can apply to a TN visa

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.820
if you have a bachelor's degree

00:16:13.825 --> 00:16:16.035
and by working on certain professional industries

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:18.380
like tech industry,

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.140
so that you can work at the US

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:24.000
Requirements are not that much

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.900
and it is easier to get this visa than other visas for other countries

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.100
In my case, I got my visa as a Colombian, for which I applied for a visa called H1B.

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:33.980
Basically you participate in a lottery

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.040
and basically you need to have

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:40.740
a bachelor's degree and certain amount of working experience

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:43.200
so that you can apply to that kind of visa.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:47.380
There are other options, for example, there's the L1 visa

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:48.060
 

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:52.460
I think basically this is a visa that you get if you work for a company

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.680
that has branches in different countries

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:58.420
and such company has a branch in the US

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:00.860
it is possible, after working for a specific amount of time in this company

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:03.380
they can move you from one country to another.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:08.100
So it can be possible that they transfer you from your country of origin where you are located

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:11.600
to the United States, so that's another of the existing methods.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:17.320
there's another possibility that I haven't personally confirmed but

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:21.200
I've been told this can be an option.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:21.700
 

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:25.580
this needs more investigation, but essentially it is to come to the US as a student

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:29.000
and while studying here, look for the possibility to get a work permit.

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:32.640
of course you have to do your own research

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.520
with a lawyer or someone that can confirm

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.580
because immigration laws can be really broad

00:17:38.585 --> 00:17:41.600
and they're always changing

00:17:41.605 --> 00:17:44.135
so you always have to ask for help

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.880
to understand the whole process.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.440
As an individual who is simply here for work

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.180
I recommend that you look what are the options

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:55.205
and look for a company that will support you with

00:17:55.205 --> 00:17:58.380
all the immigration process when they offer you a job opportunity

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.580
 

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:03.600
 

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.520
what advice could I give to people who'd like to

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.780
work here at the US and

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:11.780
specifically in techology?

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:14.800
The first one is mostly when you are speaking english

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:16.900
or want to improve your english

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.540
Take in consideration that the important thing is to communicate and

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:22.520
if you can sustain a conversation

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.040
that is enough.

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:27.940
Don't be afraid to start taking interviews,

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:30.840
if your english is not perfect, if it's not a native english, but

00:18:30.845 --> 00:18:33.665
you are able to hold conversation,

00:18:33.665 --> 00:18:36.300
a technical conversation.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.840
Even if you speak slow, even if you speak with a few mistakes.

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:41.900
If the other person can understand what you are trying to say,

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.440
Then that means you made it.

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:45.380
Go ahead

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:50.075
Second tip is that you should know what are the requirements, or at least

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:53.180
inquire on the requirements for applying to a visa.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:56.040
Depending of your country of origin, there may be different types of visas you may apply

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:58.975
and it is worth looking into it.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:02.060
In my case I would have been able to apply for a TN visa

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:05.300
which is only available for Mexico and Canada.

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.380
But there is another kind of visa like the H1B

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:12.100
that allows you to work here in the US

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:12.600
 

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:16.240
But that one has different requirements, so we have to look them up and learn them

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:20.220
so that we know what we need, this can vary depending on the country

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.700
it can even vary depending on the kind of profession you have.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:24.220
 

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:27.580
The third tip that I'll give for when

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:30.275
you want to come to work at the US

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:31.320
this one is quite personal

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:35.100
is that you need know very well

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:38.160
what kind of company you want to work for.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.500
Generally there are going to be companies

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.555
like the ones I wanted to work for

00:19:43.555 --> 00:19:46.065
big companies

00:19:46.065 --> 00:19:48.905
companies that help you with all of the immigration process

00:19:48.905 --> 00:19:49.900
 

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:52.800
companies that give you certain recognition

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.665
that you know that they are going to support you

00:19:55.665 --> 00:20:00.020
and will help you on everything you need

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:01.240
 

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.100
I would recommend to look for companies like that

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:07.360
but there is also a great number of companies that try to

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:10.565
sponsor, to help

00:20:10.565 --> 00:20:13.435
make possible for you to come here

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.360
by following the process to get a visa.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.360
So you have to look for companies that provide sponsorship

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:22.280
it doesn't have to be the biggest

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.940
or the best company.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:27.540
And also you have to be passionate about what you want to do

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.760
because when you come here you come with a commitment

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:36.120
to be in the company for certain period of time, because they make an investment in you.

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:36.615
 

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:38.860
And basically all that, relocating you

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:42.520
is a bet, that you must make worth it for the company

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:43.480
 

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:47.140
So look up what are the companies that you'd like to work for and

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:50.220
also support you on this

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.960
once you find those companies,

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.380
its time to start applying

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.540
Also don't be afraid,

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:00.360
it's just another country

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.300
it's not like a super radical change.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:05.740
It is just a change, but

00:21:05.745 --> 00:21:08.835
we are human and we can adapt to almost any situation, so there's no need to be afraid.

